hi this is pressure Locker in this video  I'll teach you a math trick so that you  can multiply any number by eleven in  your head you probably already know how  to multiply a single digit number by  eleven you simply write the number two  times and that's how you multiply the  number by eleven but what if you want to  multiply a two-digit number by eleven  the trick involves three steps first you  copy the first digit of the number the  second step is to add the two digits of  the number then you copy the last digit  of the number and that's your answer  seventeen times eleven is 187 to do  twenty-six times eleven we first copy  over the first digit then we take 2 plus  6 is 8 and then we copy the last digit  of the number to do 52 by eleven we copy  the first digit of the number five then  we take five plus two as our next number  and then we copy the last digit to get  572 478 times eleven we copy the first  digit of the number to get seven then we  need to do seven plus eight this number  is 15 so we need to write it as one and  five we then copy over the last digit of  the number eight now we need to take  care of the 1 by carrying it over to the  7 so we're going to delete the 7 and  make it eight and that's our answer  858 let's do another example of carrying  over 49 times eleven we copy over the  four then we do four plus nine is 13 and  finally we copy over the nine to account  for the carry over one we turn the 4  into a five let's say we want to  multiply a three digit number or larger  number it's exactly the same steps we're  going to copy over the first and last  digit numbers and we're going to add the  numbers that are in between so for 123  times 11 we  copy over the 1 then we take one plus  two as our next digit to get three then  we take 2 plus 3 which is 5 and finally  we copy over the last digit we could do  this for any size number we want we  first copy over the first stage of the  number then we add up the digits that  are in between so we take 1 plus 5 to  get 6 5 plus 3 to get 8 3 plus 4 is 7 4  plus 2 is 6 and finally we copy over the  last digit  here's a short proof of why the trick  works when we multiply a number by 11  that's the same thing as multiplying it  by 10 plus 1 we can write this in  another way as ABCD 0 plus ABCD now it's  very easy to see if we add up column by  column that the result is a a plus b b  plus c c plus d and d which is exactly  the trick we've been using i hope you  like this video please subscribe to my  channel i make videos on math and game  theory you can support mind your  decisions on patreon where you'll get  exclusive rewards you can also catch us  on our blog bind your decisions on  twitter at pressure Walker or get our  books at Amazon
 

